You are an expert at scheduling meetings. You are given a few constraints on the existing schedule of each participant, the meeting duration, and possibly some preferences on the meeting time. Note there exists a solution that works with existing schedule of every participant. Here are a few example tasks and solutions:

TASK: You need to schedule a meeting for Tyler, Kelly, Stephanie, Hannah, Joe, Diana and Deborah for half an hour between the work hours of 9:00 to 17:00 on Monday. 

Here are the existing schedules for everyone during the day: 
Tyler is free the entire day.
Kellyhas no meetings the whole day.
Stephanie has blocked their calendar on Monday during 11:00 to 11:30, 14:30 to 15:00; 
Hannahhas no meetings the whole day.
Joe has blocked their calendar on Monday during 9:00 to 9:30, 10:00 to 12:00, 12:30 to 13:00, 14:00 to 17:00; 
Diana has meetings on Monday during 9:00 to 10:30, 11:30 to 12:00, 13:00 to 14:00, 14:30 to 15:30, 16:00 to 17:00; 
Deborah is busy on Monday during 9:00 to 10:00, 10:30 to 12:00, 12:30 to 13:00, 13:30 to 14:00, 14:30 to 15:30, 16:00 to 16:30; 

Find a time that works for everyone's schedule and constraints. 
SOLUTION:

from z3 import *

names = ["Carol", "Peter", "Arnold", "Alice", "Bob", "Eric"]
occupations = ["lawyer", "teacher", "artist", "engineer", "nurse", "doctor"]
pets = ["dog", "hamster", "rabbit", "cat", "fish", "bird"]

s = Solver()

name_pos = {n: Int(f"name_{n}") for n in names}
occ_pos = {o: Int(f"occ_{o}") for o in occupations}
pet_pos = {p: Int(f"pet_{p}") for p in pets}

for pos in (name_pos, occ_pos, pet_pos):
    s.add(Distinct(list(pos.values())))
    for v in pos.values():
        s.add(v >= 1, v <= 6)

s.add(name_pos["Carol"] == 3)
s.add(pet_pos["rabbit"] == name_pos["Carol"])
s.add(name_pos["Arnold"] == 5)
s.add(pet_pos["hamster"] != 4)
s.add(pet_pos["fish"] != 4)
s.add(pet_pos["dog"] == name_pos["Peter"])
s.add(name_pos["Eric"] == occ_pos["nurse"])
s.add(occ_pos["teacher"] == 2)
s.add(name_pos["Alice"] < pet_pos["cat"])
s.add(pet_pos["hamster"] < name_pos["Eric"])
s.add(pet_pos["fish"] != 2)
s.add(pet_pos["dog"] + 1 == occ_pos["artist"])
s.add(Abs(occ_pos["doctor"] - occ_pos["teacher"]) == 1)
s.add(name_pos["Bob"] == pet_pos["fish"])
s.add(occ_pos["lawyer"] == pet_pos["hamster"])

if s.check() == sat:
    m = s.model()

    def house_of(var):
        return m.eval(var, model_completion=True).as_long()

    name_at = {}
    occ_at = {}
    pet_at = {}

    for h in range(1, 7):
        for n in names:
            if house_of(name_pos[n]) == h:
                name_at[h] = n
        for o in occupations:
            if house_of(occ_pos[o]) == h:
                occ_at[h] = o
        for p in pets:
            if house_of(pet_pos[p]) == h:
                pet_at[h] = p

    for h in range(1, 7):
        print(f"House {h}: {name_at[h]}, {occ_at[h]}, {pet_at[h]}")

